<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-LEOPARDSTOWN BIG RACE RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-LEOPARDSTOWN BIG RACE RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Grade One Denny Gold</p>
<p>Medal Chase at Leopardstown on Thursday, for four-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards, run over two miles one furlong (3.4 km).</p>
<p>1. Danoli  5-2 joint favourite (ridden by  Tommy Treacy)   </p>
<p>2. Land Afar (3-1) Jamie Osborne</p>
<p>3. Beakstown (20-1) Garreth Cotter</p>
<p>Nine ran.</p>
<p>Distances: six lengths, one length</p>
<p>Winner owned by Dan O'Neill and trained by Tom Foley in</p>
<p>Ireland.</p>
<p>Joint favourite: Jeffell.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 35,000 Irish pounds ($58,000)</p>
</text>
